#### Error Handling Flow

**Scenario: Partial Service Failure**

```json
// Example: 4 of 5 services succeed, Provider Service fails
{
  "memberId": "12345",
  "member": { "name": "John Doe", "dob": "1980-01-15" },
  "eligibility": { "planId": "IL-MEDICAID-001", "status": "active" },
  "claims": [ /* recent claims */ ],
  "providers": null,  // Failed service
  "errors": [
    {
      "service": "provider-service",
      "code": "SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE",
      "message": "Provider service temporarily unavailable",
      "retryAfter": 30
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "completeness": "80%",
    "requestId": "abc-123-def-456"
  }
}
```

Client receives partial data and can display available information with indication that provider data is temporarily unavailable.

